window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b309-14db5d36d55bc27e.json"]={sha256:"14db5d36d55bc27e912ddaf968d06705ba866feb5ab1a73709bbe4c505417129",value:{"id":"b309","title":"九州新幹線","titleEn":"Kyushu Shinkansen","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以九州新幹線分期連接的歷史為背景，建立坡道、橋梁與城市車站交替的教學路線。學徒要比較爬坡功率和下坡制動的能量流向，並在地震、短時暴雨與設備停機時安排可驗證的降級營運。","summaryEn":"Use the staged connection of the Kyushu Shinkansen to construct a teaching route alternating gradients, bridges and urban stops. Compare energy flow during climbing and downhill braking. Define verifiable degraded operation under an earthquake warning, short intense rainfall and equipment downtime, rather than treating rated traction power as evidence that every disrupted movement remains feasible.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-highspeed","subcategoryTitle":"高速鐵路系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"High-speed rail systems","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-highspeed","learningTags":["rail","rail-highspeed","rail"],"architectureFamily":"rail-system","architectureNodes":[["路線與土建","Alignment and civil works"],["車輛與接觸","Vehicle and contact"],["牽引供電","Traction supply"],["行車控制","Movement control"],["車站與旅客","Stations and passengers"],["監測與維護","Monitoring and maintenance"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,1],[3,4],[4,5],[5,0],[5,3]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-system","labels":["路線與土建","車輛與接觸","牽引供電","行車控制","車站與旅客"],"labelsEn":["Alignment and civil works","Vehicle and contact","Traction supply","Movement control","Stations and passengers"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合原創算例：單元 1 得 climbing=2377.944 kW；單元 2 得 traction=163.62 kN；單元 3 得 recovered=13.67708 kWh。上述三個結果使用各單元明示的不同邊界，不能任意相加或視為實際工程實測值。以第一單元 mass 的擾動測試，結果改為 2615.738 kW；學徒需先比較單位、敏感度和假設，再決定是否要細化模型。以九州新幹線分期連接的歷史為背景，建立坡道、橋梁與城市車站交替的教學路線。學徒要比較爬坡功率和下坡制動的能量流向，並在地震、短時暴雨與設備停機時安排可驗證的降級營運。 最終交付應保留原始輸入、測點時間戳、誤差範圍與無法由簡化式證明的結論。","textEn":"Integrated original exercise: unit 1 gives climbing=2377.944 kW; unit 2 gives traction=163.62 kN; unit 3 gives recovered=13.67708 kWh. These three results use different explicit boundaries and must not be added or presented as measurements of the real railway. Perturbing mass in the first unit changes its result to 2615.738 kW. Compare units, sensitivity and assumptions before deciding which model needs refinement. Use the staged connection of the Kyushu Shinkansen to construct a teaching route alternating gradients, bridges and urban stops. Compare energy flow during climbing and downhill braking. Define verifiable degraded operation under an earthquake warning, short intense rainfall and equipment downtime, rather than treating rated traction power as evidence that every disrupted movement remains feasible. The final submission should retain original inputs, measurement timestamps, uncertainty ranges and conclusions that the simplified expressions cannot establish.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b309-v16-s1","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率與黏著限制與可用牽引力","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power & Adhesion limit and usable traction","description":"本階段聚焦「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」與「黏著限制與可用牽引力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Gradient resistance and climbing power\" and \"Adhesion limit and usable traction\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b309-v16-01","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」如何影響九州新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gradient resistance and climbing power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kyushu Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"列車爬坡需提高重力位能，坡度小時沿線重力分量約等於重量乘坡度。功率還與速度相乘，因此相同牽引力下高速爬坡更耗功率；下坡則需處理持續制動能量而非僅一次停車。 坡度以升高量除以水平距離表示，百分比與小數不可混用。此項只表示重力位能增加的速率，總牽引功率還要加上加速、滾動、氣動及轉換損失。 在同一坡道比較滿載與輕載的重力功率需求。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Climbing raises gravitational potential energy. For small gradients, the along-track gravity force is approximately weight times gradient. Multiplication by speed gives power, making faster climbing more demanding at equal force; descending requires continuous energy management rather than merely one stopping event. Gradient is rise divided by horizontal distance, so percentage and decimal representations must not be mixed. This term only gives the rate of gravitational potential-energy increase. Total traction demand also includes acceleration, rolling resistance, aerodynamics and conversion losses. Compare gravitational power demand for loaded and lightly loaded trains on one gradient. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gradient resistance and climbing power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=303000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s；計算：climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2377.944 kW。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=303000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s; calculation: climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2377.944 kW.","failure":"常見誤解：「長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gradient resistance and climbing power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-01-k1","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power","text":"列車爬坡需提高重力位能，坡度小時沿線重力分量約等於重量乘坡度。功率還與速度相乘，因此相同牽引力下高速爬坡更耗功率；下坡則需處理持續制動能量而非僅一次停車。","textEn":"Climbing raises gravitational potential energy. For small gradients, the along-track gravity force is approximately weight times gradient.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gradient resistance and climbing power\" is correct?","options":["長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動","列車爬坡需提高重力位能，坡度小時沿線重力分量約等於重量乘坡度。","電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著"],"optionsEn":["One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent.","Climbing raises gravitational potential energy.","A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"列車爬坡需提高重力位能，坡度小時沿線重力分量約等於重量乘坡度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Climbing raises gravitational potential energy. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b309-v16-02","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率：定量估算","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gradient resistance and climbing power” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=303000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s；計算：climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2377.944 kW。敏感度：mass 單獨增加百分之十至 333300 kg，其餘固定，結果為 2615.738 kW。模型邊界：小坡度且定速；不含空阻、輪阻、加速與傳動損失。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=303000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s; calculation: climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2377.944 kW. Sensitivity: mass, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 333300 kg, with all other inputs fixed, gives 2615.738 kW. Model boundary: Small gradient and constant speed; aerodynamic drag, rolling resistance, acceleration and drive losses are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以路線縱斷面和列車速度重建位能變化，對照受電功率積分；坡度資料與里程基準必須一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconstruct potential-energy change from the vertical alignment and train speed, compare it with integrated line power, and keep gradient and distance datums consistent.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=303000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s；計算：climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2377.944 kW。敏感度：mass 單獨增加百分之十至 333300 kg，其餘固定，結果為 2615.738 kW。模型邊界：小坡度且定速；不含空阻、輪阻、加速與傳動損失。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=303000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s; calculation: climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2377.944 kW. Sensitivity: mass, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 333300 kg, with all other inputs fixed, gives 2615.738 kW. Model boundary: Small gradient and constant speed; aerodynamic drag, rolling resistance, acceleration and drive losses are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gradient resistance and climbing power\", which statement holds?","options":["煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點","地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=303000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots.","A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=303000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s；計算：climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2377.944 kW。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=303000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s; calculation: climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2377.944 kW. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b309-v16-03","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gradient resistance and climbing power” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以路線縱斷面和列車速度重建位能變化，對照受電功率積分；坡度資料與里程基準必須一致。 由高程剖面核對坡度，使用同一時間窗比對速度與牽引功率，另列非重力負載。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconstruct potential-energy change from the vertical alignment and train speed, compare it with integrated line power, and keep gradient and distance datums consistent. Check gradient from the elevation profile, compare speed and traction power over one time window, and list non-gravitational loads separately. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用相同高差設計長緩坡與短陡坡，對比理想位能和峰值功率，指出兩者為何不能用同一項設備額定值評估。 再以本單元 mass 的對照值重算 climbing，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Design a long gentle and short steep climb with equal height gain, compare ideal energy and peak power, and explain why one equipment rating cannot evaluate both. Also recalculate climbing for the alternative mass value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略長下坡持續熱負荷會把短時煞車能力誤當連續能力；坡度正負號錯誤則會把耗能段當成回收段。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring sustained downhill heat confuses short-term braking capability with continuous rating; a gradient-sign error can mislabel an energy-consuming section as regenerative. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以路線縱斷面和列車速度重建位能變化，對照受電功率積分；坡度資料與里程基準必須一致。 由高程剖面核對坡度，使用同一時間窗比對速度與牽引功率，另列非重力負載。","textEn":"Reconstruct potential-energy change from the vertical alignment and train speed, compare it with integrated line power, and keep gradient and distance datums consistent. Check gradient from the elevation profile, compare speed and traction power over one time window, and list non-gravitational loads separately.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用相同高差設計長緩坡與短陡坡，對比理想位能和峰值功率，指出兩者為何不能用同一項設備額定值評估。 再以本單元 mass 的對照值重算 climbing，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Design a long gentle and short steep climb with equal height gain, compare ideal energy and peak power, and explain why one equipment rating cannot evaluate both. Also recalculate climbing for the alternative mass value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gradient resistance and climbing power\"?","options":["以路線縱斷面和列車速度重建位能變化，對照受電功率積分；坡度資料與里程基準必須一致。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位"],"optionsEn":["Reconstruct potential-energy change from the vertical alignment and train speed, compare it with integrated line power, and keep gradient and distance datums consistent.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以路線縱斷面和列車速度重建位能變化，對照受電功率積分；坡度資料與里程基準必須一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconstruct potential-energy change from the vertical alignment and train speed, compare it with integrated line power, and keep gradient and distance datums consistent. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b309-v16-04","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gradient resistance and climbing power” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略長下坡持續熱負荷會把短時煞車能力誤當連續能力；坡度正負號錯誤則會把耗能段當成回收段。 功率不足時須分辨坡度阻力與黏著限制，不能只加大電流。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring sustained downhill heat confuses short-term braking capability with continuous rating; a gradient-sign error can mislabel an energy-consuming section as regenerative. When power is insufficient, distinguish gradient resistance from adhesion limits rather than only increasing current. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在同一坡道比較滿載與輕載的重力功率需求。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare gravitational power demand for loaded and lightly loaded trains on one gradient.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略長下坡持續熱負荷會把短時煞車能力誤當連續能力；坡度正負號錯誤則會把耗能段當成回收段。 功率不足時須分辨坡度阻力與黏著限制，不能只加大電流。","textEn":"Ignoring sustained downhill heat confuses short-term braking capability with continuous rating; a gradient-sign error can mislabel an energy-consuming section as regenerative. When power is insufficient, distinguish gradient resistance from adhesion limits rather than only increasing current.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gradient resistance and climbing power\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","忽略長下坡持續熱負荷會把短時煞車能力誤當連續能力；坡度正負號錯誤則會把耗能段當成回收段。","電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Ignoring sustained downhill heat confuses short-term braking capability with continuous rating.","A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"忽略長下坡持續熱負荷會把短時煞車能力誤當連續能力；坡度正負號錯誤則會把耗能段當成回收段。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring sustained downhill heat confuses short-term braking capability with continuous rating; a gradient-sign error can mislabel an energy-consuming section as regenerative. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b309-v16-05","title":"黏著限制與可用牽引力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Adhesion limit and usable traction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「黏著限制與可用牽引力」如何影響九州新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Adhesion limit and usable traction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kyushu Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"牽引力需要透過接觸斑傳到軌道，簡化上限與黏著係數及動輪法向力相乘。電機能提供更大扭矩不代表輪軌能傳遞；雨水、落葉與速度都會改變接觸狀態，使固定係數模型失去精度。 法向荷重應只取實際驅動接觸點的總量，不能自動使用整列重量。此上限也不描述黏著峰後的滑移控制；若輪重轉移，就要以每個接觸點重新分配。 檢查坡道起步時動輪荷重和接觸狀態能否傳遞要求牽引力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「黏著限制與可用牽引力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Traction reaches the track through contact patches. A simple upper bound multiplies adhesion coefficient by normal force on driven wheels. More motor torque does not guarantee more transmitted force; rain, leaves and speed alter contact conditions and limit the accuracy of a fixed coefficient. Normal load must include only the driven contacts, not automatically the weight of the whole train. This bound does not describe slip control beyond the adhesion peak. Wheel-load transfer requires a new allocation across individual contact points. Check whether driven-wheel load and contact condition can transmit the requested force during a gradient start. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Adhesion limit and usable traction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mu=0.1818 1; weight=900000 N；計算：traction=mu*weight/1000=163.62 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mu=0.1818 1; weight=900000 N; calculation: traction=mu*weight/1000=163.62 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「黏著限制與可用牽引力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Adhesion limit and usable traction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-05-k1","title":"黏著限制與可用牽引力","titleEn":"Adhesion limit and usable traction","text":"牽引力需要透過接觸斑傳到軌道，簡化上限與黏著係數及動輪法向力相乘。電機能提供更大扭矩不代表輪軌能傳遞；雨水、落葉與速度都會改變接觸狀態，使固定係數模型失去精度。","textEn":"Traction reaches the track through contact patches. A simple upper bound multiplies adhesion coefficient by normal force on driven wheels.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「黏著限制與可用牽引力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Adhesion limit and usable traction\" is correct?","options":["電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著","只要列車裝有再生煞車全部動能都能回到電網","牽引力需要透過接觸斑傳到軌道，簡化上限與黏著係數及動輪法向力相乘。"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion.","Installing regenerative braking returns all train kinetic energy to the supply network.","Traction reaches the track through contact patches."],"answer":2,"explanation":"牽引力需要透過接觸斑傳到軌道，簡化上限與黏著係數及動輪法向力相乘。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Traction reaches the track through contact patches. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b309-v16-06","title":"黏著限制與可用牽引力：定量估算","titleEn":"Adhesion limit and usable traction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「黏著限制與可用牽引力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Adhesion limit and usable traction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mu=0.1818 1; weight=900000 N；計算：traction=mu*weight/1000=163.62 kN。敏感度：mu 單獨增加百分之十至 0.19998 1，其餘固定，結果為 179.982 kN。模型邊界：準靜態庫倫上限與均勻輪重；未建模蠕滑曲線及動態減載。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mu=0.1818 1; weight=900000 N; calculation: traction=mu*weight/1000=163.62 kN. Sensitivity: mu, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.19998 1, with all other inputs fixed, gives 179.982 kN. Model boundary: Quasi-static Coulomb bound with uniform wheel load; creep curves and dynamic unloading are not modelled. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較輪速、列車獨立速度與牽引電流，找出滑轉開始點；濕乾條件必須分組，不能用全日平均係數掩蓋低黏著尾端。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare wheel speed, independently measured train speed and traction current to locate slip onset, separating wet and dry conditions rather than hiding low-adhesion tails in a daily mean.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mu=0.1818 1; weight=900000 N；計算：traction=mu*weight/1000=163.62 kN。敏感度：mu 單獨增加百分之十至 0.19998 1，其餘固定，結果為 179.982 kN。模型邊界：準靜態庫倫上限與均勻輪重；未建模蠕滑曲線及動態減載。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mu=0.1818 1; weight=900000 N; calculation: traction=mu*weight/1000=163.62 kN. Sensitivity: mu, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.19998 1, with all other inputs fixed, gives 179.982 kN. Model boundary: Quasi-static Coulomb bound with uniform wheel load; creep curves and dynamic unloading are not modelled.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「黏著限制與可用牽引力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Adhesion limit and usable traction\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mu=0.1818 1; weight=900000 N。","任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mu=0.1818 1; weight=900000 N；計算：traction=mu*weight/1000=163.62 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mu=0.1818 1; weight=900000 N; calculation: traction=mu*weight/1000=163.62 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b309-v16-07","title":"黏著限制與可用牽引力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Adhesion limit and usable traction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「黏著限制與可用牽引力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Adhesion limit and usable traction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較輪速、列車獨立速度與牽引電流，找出滑轉開始點；濕乾條件必須分組，不能用全日平均係數掩蓋低黏著尾端。 以獨立地速校對輪周速度，核實輪徑設定，再按乾濕條件與軸荷分類比對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare wheel speed, independently measured train speed and traction current to locate slip onset, separating wet and dry conditions rather than hiding low-adhesion tails in a daily mean. Calibrate wheel-periphery speed against independent ground speed, verify wheel-diameter settings, and compare results by wetness condition and axle load. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把黏著係數減半並比較動輪荷重調整，計算牽引上限，解釋為何撒砂或控制策略的效果需用試驗而不能只看馬達功率。 再以本單元 mu 的對照值重算 traction，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Halve adhesion and compare a change in driven-wheel load, calculate traction bounds, and explain why sanding or control performance requires tests rather than motor-power data alone. Also recalculate traction for the alternative mu value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：只提高扭矩可能觸發滑轉並降低可控牽引；輪徑設定誤差也會製造假的滑差，需以獨立地速判別。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Increasing torque can trigger slip and reduce controllable traction; an incorrect wheel diameter also creates apparent slip, requiring independent ground-speed evidence. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較輪速、列車獨立速度與牽引電流，找出滑轉開始點；濕乾條件必須分組，不能用全日平均係數掩蓋低黏著尾端。 以獨立地速校對輪周速度，核實輪徑設定，再按乾濕條件與軸荷分類比對。","textEn":"Compare wheel speed, independently measured train speed and traction current to locate slip onset, separating wet and dry conditions rather than hiding low-adhesion tails in a daily mean. Calibrate wheel-periphery speed against independent ground speed, verify wheel-diameter settings, and compare results by wetness condition and axle load.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把黏著係數減半並比較動輪荷重調整，計算牽引上限，解釋為何撒砂或控制策略的效果需用試驗而不能只看馬達功率。 再以本單元 mu 的對照值重算 traction，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Halve adhesion and compare a change in driven-wheel load, calculate traction bounds, and explain why sanding or control performance requires tests rather than motor-power data alone. Also recalculate traction for the alternative mu value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「黏著限制與可用牽引力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Adhesion limit and usable traction\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較輪速、列車獨立速度與牽引電流，找出滑轉開始點；濕乾條件必須分組，不能用全日平均係數掩蓋低黏著尾端。","量到變電所輸出電壓正常就代表所有列車端電壓正常"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Compare wheel speed, independently measured train speed and traction current to locate slip onset, separating wet and dry conditions rather than hiding low-adhesion tails in a daily mean.","Normal substation output voltage proves that every train receives normal voltage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較輪速、列車獨立速度與牽引電流，找出滑轉開始點；濕乾條件必須分組，不能用全日平均係數掩蓋低黏著尾端。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare wheel speed, independently measured train speed and traction current to locate slip onset, separating wet and dry conditions rather than hiding low-adhesion tails in a daily mean. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b309-v16-08","title":"黏著限制與可用牽引力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Adhesion limit and usable traction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「黏著限制與可用牽引力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Adhesion limit and usable traction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只提高扭矩可能觸發滑轉並降低可控牽引；輪徑設定誤差也會製造假的滑差，需以獨立地速判別。 先查輪徑與地速誤差，避免把量測偏差當成真滑轉。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Increasing torque can trigger slip and reduce controllable traction; an incorrect wheel diameter also creates apparent slip, requiring independent ground-speed evidence. Check diameter and ground-speed errors before interpreting measurement bias as actual wheel slip. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：檢查坡道起步時動輪荷重和接觸狀態能否傳遞要求牽引力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Check whether driven-wheel load and contact condition can transmit the requested force during a gradient start.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只提高扭矩可能觸發滑轉並降低可控牽引；輪徑設定誤差也會製造假的滑差，需以獨立地速判別。 先查輪徑與地速誤差，避免把量測偏差當成真滑轉。","textEn":"Increasing torque can trigger slip and reduce controllable traction; an incorrect wheel diameter also creates apparent slip, requiring independent ground-speed evidence. Check diameter and ground-speed errors before interpreting measurement bias as actual wheel slip.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「黏著限制與可用牽引力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Adhesion limit and usable traction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要列車裝有再生煞車全部動能都能回到電網","只提高扭矩可能觸發滑轉並降低可控牽引；輪徑設定誤差也會製造假的滑差，需以獨立地速判別。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Installing regenerative braking returns all train kinetic energy to the supply network.","Increasing torque can trigger slip and reduce controllable traction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只提高扭矩可能觸發滑轉並降低可控牽引；輪徑設定誤差也會製造假的滑差，需以獨立地速判別。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Increasing torque can trigger slip and reduce controllable traction; an incorrect wheel diameter also creates apparent slip, requiring independent ground-speed evidence. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b309-v16-s2","title":"再生煞車能量與受電條件與煞車熱量與溫升","titleEn":"Regenerative energy and receptivity & Brake heat and temperature rise","description":"本階段聚焦「再生煞車能量與受電條件」與「煞車熱量與溫升」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Regenerative energy and receptivity\" and \"Brake heat and temperature rise\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b309-v16-09","title":"再生煞車能量與受電條件：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Regenerative energy and receptivity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「再生煞車能量與受電條件」如何影響九州新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Regenerative energy and receptivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kyushu Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"煞車可回收的能量上限來自列車動能，但電網是否能接受能量、逆變器效率與輔助負載會改變實際回送量。把機械可回收量和變電站收到的電量分開，才不會把理想效率當成節電實績。 效率係數應涵蓋已宣告的轉換鏈；若把網路接受率也納入，必須說明觀測時間窗。只從速度差估計可回收量，不能辨認能量流向電網、電阻或輔助設備。 把下坡能量回送與電網可接受時段對齊，另列剩餘摩擦熱。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「再生煞車能量與受電條件」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Train kinetic energy sets an upper bound on regenerative recovery, but network receptivity, converter efficiency and auxiliary demand determine actual delivery. Separating mechanically recoverable energy from electricity received at a substation prevents ideal efficiency from being reported as measured savings. The efficiency must cover a declared conversion chain. If it includes network receptivity, the observation window must be stated. A speed change alone cannot identify how energy divides among the supply network, braking resistors and auxiliary equipment. Align downhill regenerative export with receptive intervals and separately record remaining friction heat. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Regenerative energy and receptivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=242400 kg; v=25 m/s; eta=0.65 1；計算：recovered=0.5*mass*v*v*eta/3.6e6=13.67708 kWh。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=242400 kg; v=25 m/s; eta=0.65 1; calculation: recovered=0.5*mass*v*v*eta/3.6e6=13.67708 kWh.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要列車裝有再生煞車全部動能都能回到電網」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Installing regenerative braking returns all train kinetic energy to the supply network.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「再生煞車能量與受電條件」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Regenerative energy and receptivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-09-k1","title":"再生煞車能量與受電條件","titleEn":"Regenerative energy and receptivity","text":"煞車可回收的能量上限來自列車動能，但電網是否能接受能量、逆變器效率與輔助負載會改變實際回送量。把機械可回收量和變電站收到的電量分開，才不會把理想效率當成節電實績。","textEn":"Train kinetic energy sets an upper bound on regenerative recovery, but network receptivity, converter efficiency and auxiliary demand determine actual delivery. Separating mechanically recoverable energy from electricity received at a substation prevents ideal efficiency from being reported as measured savings.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要列車裝有再生煞車全部動能都能回到電網 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Installing regenerative braking returns all train kinetic energy to the supply network. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「再生煞車能量與受電條件」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Regenerative energy and receptivity\" is correct?","options":["煞車可回收的能量上限來自列車動能，但電網是否能接受能量、逆變器效率與輔助負載會改變實際回送量。","只要列車裝有再生煞車全部動能都能回到電網","煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點"],"optionsEn":["Train kinetic energy sets an upper bound on regenerative recovery, but network receptivity, converter efficiency and auxiliary demand determine actual delivery.","Installing regenerative braking returns all train kinetic energy to the supply network.","A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots."],"answer":0,"explanation":"煞車可回收的能量上限來自列車動能，但電網是否能接受能量、逆變器效率與輔助負載會改變實際回送量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Train kinetic energy sets an upper bound on regenerative recovery, but network receptivity, converter efficiency and auxiliary demand determine actual delivery. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b309-v16-10","title":"再生煞車能量與受電條件：定量估算","titleEn":"Regenerative energy and receptivity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「再生煞車能量與受電條件」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Regenerative energy and receptivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=242400 kg; v=25 m/s; eta=0.65 1；計算：recovered=0.5*mass*v*v*eta/3.6e6=13.67708 kWh。敏感度：mass 單獨增加百分之十至 266640 kg，其餘固定，結果為 15.04479 kWh。模型邊界：一次水平減速、固定總效率；不含阻力及架線電壓限制導致的截斷。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=242400 kg; v=25 m/s; eta=0.65 1; calculation: recovered=0.5*mass*v*v*eta/3.6e6=13.67708 kWh. Sensitivity: mass, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 266640 kg, with all other inputs fixed, gives 15.04479 kWh. Model boundary: One level deceleration with fixed overall efficiency; resistance and voltage-limited curtailment are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步積分直流鏈、受電端與制動電阻的功率，對照初末速度；將輔助用電和回送電量用一致符號處理。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Integrate DC-link, line-side and braking-resistor power synchronously and compare initial and final speeds, treating auxiliary consumption and exported energy with consistent signs.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=242400 kg; v=25 m/s; eta=0.65 1；計算：recovered=0.5*mass*v*v*eta/3.6e6=13.67708 kWh。敏感度：mass 單獨增加百分之十至 266640 kg，其餘固定，結果為 15.04479 kWh。模型邊界：一次水平減速、固定總效率；不含阻力及架線電壓限制導致的截斷。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=242400 kg; v=25 m/s; eta=0.65 1; calculation: recovered=0.5*mass*v*v*eta/3.6e6=13.67708 kWh. Sensitivity: mass, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 266640 kg, with all other inputs fixed, gives 15.04479 kWh. Model boundary: One level deceleration with fixed overall efficiency; resistance and voltage-limited curtailment are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「再生煞車能量與受電條件」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Regenerative energy and receptivity\", which statement holds?","options":["地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=242400 kg; v=25 m/s; eta=0.65 1。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位"],"optionsEn":["A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.","Original hypothetical exercise.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=242400 kg; v=25 m/s; eta=0.65 1；計算：recovered=0.5*mass*v*v*eta/3.6e6=13.67708 kWh。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=242400 kg; v=25 m/s; eta=0.65 1; calculation: recovered=0.5*mass*v*v*eta/3.6e6=13.67708 kWh. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b309-v16-11","title":"再生煞車能量與受電條件：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Regenerative energy and receptivity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「再生煞車能量與受電條件」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Regenerative energy and receptivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步積分直流鏈、受電端與制動電阻的功率，對照初末速度；將輔助用電和回送電量用一致符號處理。 檢查功率計正負方向與積分時間邊界，以能量平衡殘差確認回送量未被重複計入。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Integrate DC-link, line-side and braking-resistor power synchronously and compare initial and final speeds, treating auxiliary consumption and exported energy with consistent signs. Check meter polarity and integration boundaries, then use the energy-balance residual to confirm that exported energy has not been counted twice. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較有受電列車與無受電列車兩種功率時間圖，做能量收支表，提出儲能需求並說明額定能量不等於可接受功率。 再以本單元 mass 的對照值重算 recovered，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare power traces with and without a receptive train, build an energy balance, and size an illustrative storage requirement while distinguishing energy capacity from acceptable power. Also recalculate recovered for the alternative mass value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：鄰車不在受電時再生電壓可能升高而轉入電阻制動；只量逆變器端會高估真正回到供電網的能量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without a receptive neighbouring train, voltage can rise and trigger resistor braking; measurement only at the inverter can overstate energy returned to the supply network. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步積分直流鏈、受電端與制動電阻的功率，對照初末速度；將輔助用電和回送電量用一致符號處理。 檢查功率計正負方向與積分時間邊界，以能量平衡殘差確認回送量未被重複計入。","textEn":"Integrate DC-link, line-side and braking-resistor power synchronously and compare initial and final speeds, treating auxiliary consumption and exported energy with consistent signs. Check meter polarity and integration boundaries, then use the energy-balance residual to confirm that exported energy has not been counted twice.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較有受電列車與無受電列車兩種功率時間圖，做能量收支表，提出儲能需求並說明額定能量不等於可接受功率。 再以本單元 mass 的對照值重算 recovered，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare power traces with and without a receptive train, build an energy balance, and size an illustrative storage requirement while distinguishing energy capacity from acceptable power. Also recalculate recovered for the alternative mass value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「再生煞車能量與受電條件」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Regenerative energy and receptivity\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低","同步積分直流鏈、受電端與制動電阻的功率，對照初末速度；將輔助用電和回送電量用一致符號處理。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low.","Integrate DC-link, line-side and braking-resistor power synchronously and compare initial and final speeds, treating auxiliary consumption and exported energy with consistent signs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步積分直流鏈、受電端與制動電阻的功率，對照初末速度；將輔助用電和回送電量用一致符號處理。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Integrate DC-link, line-side and braking-resistor power synchronously and compare initial and final speeds, treating auxiliary consumption and exported energy with consistent signs. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b309-v16-12","title":"再生煞車能量與受電條件：失效診斷","titleEn":"Regenerative energy and receptivity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「再生煞車能量與受電條件」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Regenerative energy and receptivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"鄰車不在受電時再生電壓可能升高而轉入電阻制動；只量逆變器端會高估真正回到供電網的能量。 若回送受限，需查架線電壓及電阻制動記錄。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without a receptive neighbouring train, voltage can rise and trigger resistor braking; measurement only at the inverter can overstate energy returned to the supply network. When export is curtailed, inspect line-voltage and resistor-braking records together. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把下坡能量回送與電網可接受時段對齊，另列剩餘摩擦熱。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Align downhill regenerative export with receptive intervals and separately record remaining friction heat.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要列車裝有再生煞車全部動能都能回到電網」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Installing regenerative braking returns all train kinetic energy to the supply network.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"鄰車不在受電時再生電壓可能升高而轉入電阻制動；只量逆變器端會高估真正回到供電網的能量。 若回送受限，需查架線電壓及電阻制動記錄。","textEn":"Without a receptive neighbouring train, voltage can rise and trigger resistor braking; measurement only at the inverter can overstate energy returned to the supply network. When export is curtailed, inspect line-voltage and resistor-braking records together.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「再生煞車能量與受電條件」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Regenerative energy and receptivity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["鄰車不在受電時再生電壓可能升高而轉入電阻制動；只量逆變器端會高估真正回到供電網的能量。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點"],"optionsEn":["Without a receptive neighbouring train, voltage can rise and trigger resistor braking.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鄰車不在受電時再生電壓可能升高而轉入電阻制動；只量逆變器端會高估真正回到供電網的能量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without a receptive neighbouring train, voltage can rise and trigger resistor braking; measurement only at the inverter can overstate energy returned to the supply network. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b309-v16-13","title":"煞車熱量與溫升：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「煞車熱量與溫升」如何影響九州新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Brake heat and temperature rise” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kyushu Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"未回收的動能會在摩擦煞車與阻力路徑中轉成熱，平均溫升由分配到構件的能量除以熱容量決定。短時平均模型無法描述表面熱點、對流冷卻或熱裂紋，需要把能量分配與熱擴散分開。 有效受熱質量可以小於構件總質量，短時接觸表面的熱量也未必已傳到內部。能量平衡應先界定摩擦分配比例，再評估對流、輻射和間歇冷卻是否可忽略。 檢查連續下坡制動造成的累積熱負荷與冷卻間隔。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「煞車熱量與溫升」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Unrecovered kinetic energy becomes heat through friction brakes and resistance paths. Average temperature rise is allocated energy divided by thermal capacity. A short-duration lumped model cannot describe surface hot spots, cooling or thermal cracks; energy allocation and thermal diffusion are separate questions. The effective heated mass can be smaller than total component mass, and short-duration surface heat may not reach the interior. First define frictional energy allocation, then assess whether convection, radiation and cooling between events can be neglected. Examine cumulative heat loading and cooling intervals during repeated downhill braking. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Brake heat and temperature rise” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=1.212e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K)；計算：rise=energy/(mass*cp)=119.7628 K。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=1.212e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K); calculation: rise=energy/(mass*cp)=119.7628 K.","failure":"常見誤解：「煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「煞車熱量與溫升」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Brake heat and temperature rise”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-13-k1","title":"煞車熱量與溫升","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise","text":"未回收的動能會在摩擦煞車與阻力路徑中轉成熱，平均溫升由分配到構件的能量除以熱容量決定。短時平均模型無法描述表面熱點、對流冷卻或熱裂紋，需要把能量分配與熱擴散分開。","textEn":"Unrecovered kinetic energy becomes heat through friction brakes and resistance paths. Average temperature rise is allocated energy divided by thermal capacity.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「煞車熱量與溫升」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Brake heat and temperature rise\" is correct?","options":["煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點","未回收的動能會在摩擦煞車與阻力路徑中轉成熱，平均溫升由分配到構件的能量除以熱容量決定。","任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度"],"optionsEn":["A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots.","Unrecovered kinetic energy becomes heat through friction brakes and resistance paths.","Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"未回收的動能會在摩擦煞車與阻力路徑中轉成熱，平均溫升由分配到構件的能量除以熱容量決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Unrecovered kinetic energy becomes heat through friction brakes and resistance paths. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b309-v16-14","title":"煞車熱量與溫升：定量估算","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「煞車熱量與溫升」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Brake heat and temperature rise” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=1.212e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K)；計算：rise=energy/(mass*cp)=119.7628 K。敏感度：energy 單獨增加百分之十至 1.3332e+07 J，其餘固定，結果為 131.7391 K。模型邊界：均勻溫度且無散熱、常數比熱；不推定摩擦材極限。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=1.212e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K); calculation: rise=energy/(mass*cp)=119.7628 K. Sensitivity: energy, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1.3332e+07 J, with all other inputs fixed, gives 131.7391 K. Model boundary: Uniform temperature without heat loss and with constant heat capacity; no friction-material limit is inferred. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以熱電偶與紅外量測交叉檢查溫升，記錄煞車能量、環境溫度與冷卻時間，並校正紅外放射率。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Cross-check temperature rise with thermocouples and infrared measurements, record braking energy, ambient temperature and cooling time, and calibrate infrared emissivity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=1.212e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K)；計算：rise=energy/(mass*cp)=119.7628 K。敏感度：energy 單獨增加百分之十至 1.3332e+07 J，其餘固定，結果為 131.7391 K。模型邊界：均勻溫度且無散熱、常數比熱；不推定摩擦材極限。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=1.212e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K); calculation: rise=energy/(mass*cp)=119.7628 K. Sensitivity: energy, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1.3332e+07 J, with all other inputs fixed, gives 131.7391 K. Model boundary: Uniform temperature without heat loss and with constant heat capacity; no friction-material limit is inferred.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「煞車熱量與溫升」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Brake heat and temperature rise\", which statement holds?","options":["橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成","量到變電所輸出電壓正常就代表所有列車端電壓正常","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=1.212e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K)。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.","Normal substation output voltage proves that every train receives normal voltage.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=1.212e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K)；計算：rise=energy/(mass*cp)=119.7628 K。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=1.212e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K); calculation: rise=energy/(mass*cp)=119.7628 K. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b309-v16-15","title":"煞車熱量與溫升：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「煞車熱量與溫升」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Brake heat and temperature rise” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以熱電偶與紅外量測交叉檢查溫升，記錄煞車能量、環境溫度與冷卻時間，並校正紅外放射率。 在不同深度保留溫度曲線並核對感測器反應時間，用初末能量平衡檢查平均溫升。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Cross-check temperature rise with thermocouples and infrared measurements, record braking energy, ambient temperature and cooling time, and calibrate infrared emissivity. Retain temperature histories at different depths, verify sensor response time, and use initial-to-final energy balance to check mean temperature rise. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將同一能量分給兩種有效熱容量，計算平均溫升後設計能辨認熱點的量測網格，說明集中參數模型缺少哪些資訊。 再以本單元 energy 的對照值重算 rise，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Allocate equal energy to two effective thermal capacities, calculate average rise, and design a measurement grid for hot spots while identifying information missing from the lumped model. Also recalculate rise for the alternative energy value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：局部接觸不均會產生熱點，即使平均溫升不高仍可能形成熱裂紋；錯誤放射率也會掩蓋真實表面溫度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uneven contact can create hot spots and thermal cracks despite a modest mean rise; incorrect emissivity can also conceal the actual surface temperature. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以熱電偶與紅外量測交叉檢查溫升，記錄煞車能量、環境溫度與冷卻時間，並校正紅外放射率。 在不同深度保留溫度曲線並核對感測器反應時間，用初末能量平衡檢查平均溫升。","textEn":"Cross-check temperature rise with thermocouples and infrared measurements, record braking energy, ambient temperature and cooling time, and calibrate infrared emissivity. Retain temperature histories at different depths, verify sensor response time, and use initial-to-final energy balance to check mean temperature rise.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將同一能量分給兩種有效熱容量，計算平均溫升後設計能辨認熱點的量測網格，說明集中參數模型缺少哪些資訊。 再以本單元 energy 的對照值重算 rise，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Allocate equal energy to two effective thermal capacities, calculate average rise, and design a measurement grid for hot spots while identifying information missing from the lumped model. Also recalculate rise for the alternative energy value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「煞車熱量與溫升」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Brake heat and temperature rise\"?","options":["以熱電偶與紅外量測交叉檢查溫升，記錄煞車能量、環境溫度與冷卻時間，並校正紅外放射率。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動"],"optionsEn":["Cross-check temperature rise with thermocouples and infrared measurements, record braking energy, ambient temperature and cooling time, and calibrate infrared emissivity.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以熱電偶與紅外量測交叉檢查溫升，記錄煞車能量、環境溫度與冷卻時間，並校正紅外放射率。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Cross-check temperature rise with thermocouples and infrared measurements, record braking energy, ambient temperature and cooling time, and calibrate infrared emissivity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b309-v16-16","title":"煞車熱量與溫升：失效診斷","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「煞車熱量與溫升」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Brake heat and temperature rise” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"局部接觸不均會產生熱點，即使平均溫升不高仍可能形成熱裂紋；錯誤放射率也會掩蓋真實表面溫度。 若表面與內部溫差很大，集中熱容量假設便不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uneven contact can create hot spots and thermal cracks despite a modest mean rise; incorrect emissivity can also conceal the actual surface temperature. A large surface-to-core temperature difference indicates that the lumped thermal-capacity assumption is insufficient. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：檢查連續下坡制動造成的累積熱負荷與冷卻間隔。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Examine cumulative heat loading and cooling intervals during repeated downhill braking.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"局部接觸不均會產生熱點，即使平均溫升不高仍可能形成熱裂紋；錯誤放射率也會掩蓋真實表面溫度。 若表面與內部溫差很大，集中熱容量假設便不足。","textEn":"Uneven contact can create hot spots and thermal cracks despite a modest mean rise; incorrect emissivity can also conceal the actual surface temperature. A large surface-to-core temperature difference indicates that the lumped thermal-capacity assumption is insufficient.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「煞車熱量與溫升」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Brake heat and temperature rise\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","局部接觸不均會產生熱點，即使平均溫升不高仍可能形成熱裂紋；錯誤放射率也會掩蓋真實表面溫度。","任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Uneven contact can create hot spots and thermal cracks despite a modest mean rise; incorrect emissivity can also conceal the actual surface temperature.","Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部接觸不均會產生熱點，即使平均溫升不高仍可能形成熱裂紋；錯誤放射率也會掩蓋真實表面溫度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uneven contact can create hot spots and thermal cracks despite a modest mean rise; incorrect emissivity can also conceal the actual surface temperature. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b309-v16-s3","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度與地震偵測提前量","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration & Seismic detection lead time","description":"本階段聚焦「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」與「地震偵測提前量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cant and unbalanced acceleration\" and \"Seismic detection lead time\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b309-v16-17","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」如何影響九州新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cant and unbalanced acceleration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kyushu Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"曲線需求的向心加速度由重力沿軌道平面的分量與輪軌側向作用共同提供。超高平衡速度只對特定半徑和速度成立，慢車可能出現超高過剩；不能把增加超高當成所有車種都受益的措施。 殘餘加速度的正負表示側向作用方向，而不是安全與危險的二元判斷。半徑、軌距與高差必須使用一致長度單位，車體感受還會受到懸吊轉角影響。 在山地曲線比較通過速度與超高過剩的低速情境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"On a curve, the component of gravity in the track plane and wheel-rail lateral forces together provide centripetal acceleration. Equilibrium cant applies to one radius and speed. A slower service can experience cant excess, so increasing cant does not improve every train condition. The sign of residual acceleration identifies its lateral direction, not a binary safe-unsafe outcome. Radius, gauge and rail-level difference require consistent length units. Carbody response is additionally affected by suspension rotation, which this geometric estimate does not resolve. Compare running speed with low-speed cant excess on a mountain curve. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cant and unbalanced acceleration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=60.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m；計算：residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.13329 m/s^2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=60.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m; calculation: residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.13329 m/s^2.","failure":"常見誤解：「任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cant and unbalanced acceleration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-17-k1","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration","text":"曲線需求的向心加速度由重力沿軌道平面的分量與輪軌側向作用共同提供。超高平衡速度只對特定半徑和速度成立，慢車可能出現超高過剩；不能把增加超高當成所有車種都受益的措施。","textEn":"On a curve, the component of gravity in the track plane and wheel-rail lateral forces together provide centripetal acceleration. Equilibrium cant applies to one radius and speed.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cant and unbalanced acceleration\" is correct?","options":["任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度","地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下","曲線需求的向心加速度由重力沿軌道平面的分量與輪軌側向作用共同提供。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed.","A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.","On a curve, the component of gravity in the track plane and wheel-rail lateral forces together provide centripetal acceleration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"曲線需求的向心加速度由重力沿軌道平面的分量與輪軌側向作用共同提供。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"On a curve, the component of gravity in the track plane and wheel-rail lateral forces together provide centripetal acceleration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b309-v16-18","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度：定量估算","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cant and unbalanced acceleration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=60.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m；計算：residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.13329 m/s^2。敏感度：v 單獨增加百分之十至 66.66 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 0.3260889 m/s^2。模型邊界：小角度近似與剛性車體；未計懸吊側滾、動態輪重減載和規範允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=60.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m; calculation: residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.13329 m/s^2. Sensitivity: v, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 66.66 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.3260889 m/s^2. Model boundary: Small-angle approximation and rigid body; suspension roll, dynamic wheel unloading and acceptance limits are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在相同半徑區段量測軌面高差與橫向加速度，扣除感測器安裝角度，並把車體讀值與軌道平面讀值分開記錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure rail level difference and lateral acceleration on the same curve, remove sensor mounting angle, and distinguish carbody readings from track-plane readings.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=60.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m；計算：residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.13329 m/s^2。敏感度：v 單獨增加百分之十至 66.66 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 0.3260889 m/s^2。模型邊界：小角度近似與剛性車體；未計懸吊側滾、動態輪重減載和規範允收值。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=60.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m; calculation: residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.13329 m/s^2. Sensitivity: v, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 66.66 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.3260889 m/s^2. Model boundary: Small-angle approximation and rigid body; suspension roll, dynamic wheel unloading and acceptance limits are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cant and unbalanced acceleration\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=60.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位","設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.","High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=60.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m；計算：residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.13329 m/s^2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=60.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m; calculation: residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.13329 m/s^2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b309-v16-19","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cant and unbalanced acceleration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在相同半徑區段量測軌面高差與橫向加速度，扣除感測器安裝角度，並把車體讀值與軌道平面讀值分開記錄。 用實測半徑和高差重算平衡速度，保留感測器安裝角的校正值及量測不確定度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure rail level difference and lateral acceleration on the same curve, remove sensor mounting angle, and distinguish carbody readings from track-plane readings. Recalculate equilibrium speed from measured radius and cant, retaining mounting-angle corrections and uncertainty for the acceleration sensor. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：選兩種速度共同計算殘餘加速度，找出符號反轉位置，說明為何混合服務需要速度分布而非單一最高速度。 再以本單元 v 的對照值重算 residual，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate residual acceleration for two speeds, locate its sign reversal, and explain why mixed services require a speed distribution rather than one maximum speed. Also recalculate residual for the alternative v value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：只依高速通過最佳化超高，可能讓慢車或停車承受反向側向力；感測器橫滾又會把重力投影混入振動訊號。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Cant optimised only for fast trains can impose reverse lateral loading on slow or stopped trains; sensor roll also mixes gravity into vibration measurements. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在相同半徑區段量測軌面高差與橫向加速度，扣除感測器安裝角度，並把車體讀值與軌道平面讀值分開記錄。 用實測半徑和高差重算平衡速度，保留感測器安裝角的校正值及量測不確定度。","textEn":"Measure rail level difference and lateral acceleration on the same curve, remove sensor mounting angle, and distinguish carbody readings from track-plane readings. Recalculate equilibrium speed from measured radius and cant, retaining mounting-angle corrections and uncertainty for the acceleration sensor.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"選兩種速度共同計算殘餘加速度，找出符號反轉位置，說明為何混合服務需要速度分布而非單一最高速度。 再以本單元 v 的對照值重算 residual，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Calculate residual acceleration for two speeds, locate its sign reversal, and explain why mixed services require a speed distribution rather than one maximum speed. Also recalculate residual for the alternative v value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cant and unbalanced acceleration\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在相同半徑區段量測軌面高差與橫向加速度，扣除感測器安裝角度，並把車體讀值與軌道平面讀值分開記錄。","電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure rail level difference and lateral acceleration on the same curve, remove sensor mounting angle, and distinguish carbody readings from track-plane readings.","A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在相同半徑區段量測軌面高差與橫向加速度，扣除感測器安裝角度，並把車體讀值與軌道平面讀值分開記錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure rail level difference and lateral acceleration on the same curve, remove sensor mounting angle, and distinguish carbody readings from track-plane readings. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b309-v16-20","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cant and unbalanced acceleration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只依高速通過最佳化超高，可能讓慢車或停車承受反向側向力；感測器橫滾又會把重力投影混入振動訊號。 需核對高差符號與曲線方向，防止左右軌互換。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Cant optimised only for fast trains can impose reverse lateral loading on slow or stopped trains; sensor roll also mixes gravity into vibration measurements. Check cant sign against curve direction to prevent swapping the inner and outer rails. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在山地曲線比較通過速度與超高過剩的低速情境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare running speed with low-speed cant excess on a mountain curve.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只依高速通過最佳化超高，可能讓慢車或停車承受反向側向力；感測器橫滾又會把重力投影混入振動訊號。 需核對高差符號與曲線方向，防止左右軌互換。","textEn":"Cant optimised only for fast trains can impose reverse lateral loading on slow or stopped trains; sensor roll also mixes gravity into vibration measurements. Check cant sign against curve direction to prevent swapping the inner and outer rails.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cant and unbalanced acceleration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下","只依高速通過最佳化超高，可能讓慢車或停車承受反向側向力；感測器橫滾又會把重力投影混入振動訊號。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.","Cant optimised only for fast trains can impose reverse lateral loading on slow or stopped trains; sensor roll also mixes gravity into vibration measurements."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只依高速通過最佳化超高，可能讓慢車或停車承受反向側向力；感測器橫滾又會把重力投影混入振動訊號。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Cant optimised only for fast trains can impose reverse lateral loading on slow or stopped trains; sensor roll also mixes gravity into vibration measurements. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b309-v16-21","title":"地震偵測提前量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「地震偵測提前量」如何影響九州新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Seismic detection lead time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kyushu Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地震警報的可用提前量來自較快波到達感測點與較慢強震波到達設施之間的差，再扣掉傳輸和判定延遲。距離太近時提前量可能為負，警報並不能讓列車瞬間停止。 此處以相同距離比較兩種波速，屬簡化幾何模型。實際感測站可能不在線路與震源之間；可用時間還包括資料品質檢查及保護命令發送，不能只比較波速。 把震源距離和通訊延遲作為獨立變數，辨識預警限制。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「地震偵測提前量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Usable seismic lead time is the difference between faster-wave detection and slower damaging-wave arrival, less communication and decision delay. A nearby source may leave negative lead time. An alarm therefore cannot make a moving train stop instantaneously, even when the detection itself works correctly. The exercise compares two wave speeds over the same distance and therefore uses simplified geometry. A real sensor may not lie between the source and railway. Available time also includes data-quality checks and protection-command delivery, not only wave propagation. Treat source distance and communication delay as separate variables when identifying warning limits. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Seismic detection lead time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：distance=101000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s；計算：lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.02381 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: distance=101000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s; calculation: lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.02381 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「地震偵測提前量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Seismic detection lead time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-21-k1","title":"地震偵測提前量","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time","text":"地震警報的可用提前量來自較快波到達感測點與較慢強震波到達設施之間的差，再扣掉傳輸和判定延遲。距離太近時提前量可能為負，警報並不能讓列車瞬間停止。","textEn":"Usable seismic lead time is the difference between faster-wave detection and slower damaging-wave arrival, less communication and decision delay. A nearby source may leave negative lead time.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地震偵測提前量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Seismic detection lead time\" is correct?","options":["地震警報的可用提前量來自較快波到達感測點與較慢強震波到達設施之間的差，再扣掉傳輸和判定延遲。","地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Usable seismic lead time is the difference between faster-wave detection and slower damaging-wave arrival, less communication and decision delay.","A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"地震警報的可用提前量來自較快波到達感測點與較慢強震波到達設施之間的差，再扣掉傳輸和判定延遲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Usable seismic lead time is the difference between faster-wave detection and slower damaging-wave arrival, less communication and decision delay. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b309-v16-22","title":"地震偵測提前量：定量估算","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「地震偵測提前量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Seismic detection lead time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：distance=101000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s；計算：lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.02381 s。敏感度：distance 單獨增加百分之十至 111100 m，其餘固定，結果為 11.22619 s。模型邊界：共線源站幾何與固定波速；不預測震度或實際地震動。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: distance=101000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s; calculation: lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.02381 s. Sensitivity: distance, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 111100 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 11.22619 s. Model boundary: Collinear source-station geometry and constant wave speeds; neither intensity nor actual ground motion is predicted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用歷史或合成波形重播整條訊號鏈，記錄偵測、判定、通訊及列車接收時間，量出漏警、誤警和延遲分布。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Replay historical or synthetic waveforms through the complete chain, log detection, decision, communication and train receipt times, and measure missed alarms, false alarms and latency distribution.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：distance=101000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s；計算：lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.02381 s。敏感度：distance 單獨增加百分之十至 111100 m，其餘固定，結果為 11.22619 s。模型邊界：共線源站幾何與固定波速；不預測震度或實際地震動。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: distance=101000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s; calculation: lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.02381 s. Sensitivity: distance, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 111100 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 11.22619 s. Model boundary: Collinear source-station geometry and constant wave speeds; neither intensity nor actual ground motion is predicted.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地震偵測提前量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Seismic detection lead time\", which statement holds?","options":["量到變電所輸出電壓正常就代表所有列車端電壓正常","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：distance=101000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s。","長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動"],"optionsEn":["Normal substation output voltage proves that every train receives normal voltage.","Original hypothetical exercise.","One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：distance=101000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s；計算：lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.02381 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: distance=101000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s; calculation: lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.02381 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b309-v16-23","title":"地震偵測提前量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「地震偵測提前量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Seismic detection lead time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用歷史或合成波形重播整條訊號鏈，記錄偵測、判定、通訊及列車接收時間，量出漏警、誤警和延遲分布。 以完整訊號重播核對每個時間戳，將總延遲分解成判定、網路與列車端處理。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Replay historical or synthetic waveforms through the complete chain, log detection, decision, communication and train receipt times, and measure missed alarms, false alarms and latency distribution. Use full-chain signal replay to verify every timestamp and separate total delay into decision, network and train-side processing components. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將震源距離縮短並把通訊延遲加倍，計算剩餘提前量；與制動時間比較，提出只在模型範圍內成立的結論。 再以本單元 distance 的對照值重算 lead，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Shorten source distance and double communication delay, calculate remaining lead time, and compare it with braking time without extending the conclusion beyond the model. Also recalculate lead for the alternative distance value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：只驗證感測器觸發而不驗證下游通訊，可能高估提前量；設備共用電源也可能讓兩條名義獨立通道同時失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Testing the sensor without downstream communication overestimates lead time; a shared power supply can also defeat nominally independent channels simultaneously. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用歷史或合成波形重播整條訊號鏈，記錄偵測、判定、通訊及列車接收時間，量出漏警、誤警和延遲分布。 以完整訊號重播核對每個時間戳，將總延遲分解成判定、網路與列車端處理。","textEn":"Replay historical or synthetic waveforms through the complete chain, log detection, decision, communication and train receipt times, and measure missed alarms, false alarms and latency distribution. Use full-chain signal replay to verify every timestamp and separate total delay into decision, network and train-side processing components.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將震源距離縮短並把通訊延遲加倍，計算剩餘提前量；與制動時間比較，提出只在模型範圍內成立的結論。 再以本單元 distance 的對照值重算 lead，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Shorten source distance and double communication delay, calculate remaining lead time, and compare it with braking time without extending the conclusion beyond the model. Also recalculate lead for the alternative distance value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地震偵測提前量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Seismic detection lead time\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","只要列車裝有再生煞車全部動能都能回到電網","用歷史或合成波形重播整條訊號鏈，記錄偵測、判定、通訊及列車接收時間，量出漏警、誤警和延遲分布。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Installing regenerative braking returns all train kinetic energy to the supply network.","Replay historical or synthetic waveforms through the complete chain, log detection, decision, communication and train receipt times, and measure missed alarms, false alarms and latency distribution."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用歷史或合成波形重播整條訊號鏈，記錄偵測、判定、通訊及列車接收時間，量出漏警、誤警和延遲分布。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Replay historical or synthetic waveforms through the complete chain, log detection, decision, communication and train receipt times, and measure missed alarms, false alarms and latency distribution. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b309-v16-24","title":"地震偵測提前量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「地震偵測提前量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Seismic detection lead time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只驗證感測器觸發而不驗證下游通訊，可能高估提前量；設備共用電源也可能讓兩條名義獨立通道同時失效。 感測成功不等於制動成功，須查列車收到命令後的動作。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Testing the sensor without downstream communication overestimates lead time; a shared power supply can also defeat nominally independent channels simultaneously. Successful detection is not successful braking; inspect the train response after command receipt. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把震源距離和通訊延遲作為獨立變數，辨識預警限制。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Treat source distance and communication delay as separate variables when identifying warning limits.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只驗證感測器觸發而不驗證下游通訊，可能高估提前量；設備共用電源也可能讓兩條名義獨立通道同時失效。 感測成功不等於制動成功，須查列車收到命令後的動作。","textEn":"Testing the sensor without downstream communication overestimates lead time; a shared power supply can also defeat nominally independent channels simultaneously. Successful detection is not successful braking; inspect the train response after command receipt.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地震偵測提前量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Seismic detection lead time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只驗證感測器觸發而不驗證下游通訊，可能高估提前量；設備共用電源也可能讓兩條名義獨立通道同時失效。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Testing the sensor without downstream communication overestimates lead time.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只驗證感測器觸發而不驗證下游通訊，可能高估提前量；設備共用電源也可能讓兩條名義獨立通道同時失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Testing the sensor without downstream communication overestimates lead time; a shared power supply can also defeat nominally independent channels simultaneously. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b309-v16-s4","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度與集水與排水容量","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity & Catchment inflow and drainage capacity","description":"本階段聚焦「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」與「集水與排水容量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\" and \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b309-v16-25","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」如何影響九州新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kyushu Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。鐵道橋還需要動態與軌道相互作用檢查，靜態梁算例只用來辨認參數量級。 跨長四次方使幾何誤差特別重要，但只有在相同支承、均布荷載及截面條件下才可比較。將毫米轉成公尺後再核對剛度，可避免把量測位移誤差變成材料性能判斷。 量測橋跨與支點位移，避免把支承移動當成梁剛度改變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span. Section inertia and material stiffness jointly resist bending. A railway bridge also requires dynamic and track-interaction checks; this static beam exercise only reveals parameter magnitudes. Fourth-power span dependence makes geometry important, but comparison requires the same support, uniform-load and section assumptions. Convert millimetres and metres consistently before checking stiffness, so a displacement-unit error does not become a false conclusion about material properties. Measure span and support motion to avoid mistaking support displacement for a stiffness change. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=25.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=0.9451403 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=25.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=0.9451403 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-25-k1","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity","text":"簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。鐵道橋還需要動態與軌道相互作用檢查，靜態梁算例只用來辨認參數量級。","textEn":"For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span. Section inertia and material stiffness jointly resist bending.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\" is correct?","options":["橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成","簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位"],"optionsEn":["Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.","For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater."],"answer":1,"explanation":"簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b309-v16-26","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：定量估算","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=25.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=0.9451403 mm。敏感度：L 單獨增加百分之十至 27.775 m，其餘固定，結果為 1.38378 mm。模型邊界：簡支Euler梁、小撓度、靜態均布荷載；不代表列車移動荷載。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=25.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=0.9451403 mm. Sensitivity: L, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 27.775 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1.38378 mm. Model boundary: Simply supported Euler beam, small deflection and static uniform load; not a moving train-load analysis. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=25.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=0.9451403 mm。敏感度：L 單獨增加百分之十至 27.775 m，其餘固定，結果為 1.38378 mm。模型邊界：簡支Euler梁、小撓度、靜態均布荷載；不代表列車移動荷載。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=25.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=0.9451403 mm. Sensitivity: L, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 27.775 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1.38378 mm. Model boundary: Simply supported Euler beam, small deflection and static uniform load; not a moving train-load analysis.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\", which statement holds?","options":["設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低","電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=25.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4。"],"optionsEn":["High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low.","A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=25.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=0.9451403 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=25.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=0.9451403 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b309-v16-27","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。 先以已知荷載校對位移計量程與零點，分別記錄載入卸載路徑及支點運動。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading. Check displacement-sensor range and zero under known loading, recording loading and unloading paths separately from support movement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持截面不變增加跨長，再比較提高慣性矩的補償幅度，說明靜態位移符合預期為何仍不能取代動態驗證。 再以本單元 L 的對照值重算 deflection，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase span while keeping the section fixed, calculate the compensating inertia change, and explain why agreement in static deflection cannot replace dynamic verification. Also recalculate deflection for the alternative L value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。 先以已知荷載校對位移計量程與零點，分別記錄載入卸載路徑及支點運動。","textEn":"Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading. Check displacement-sensor range and zero under known loading, recording loading and unloading paths separately from support movement.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持截面不變增加跨長，再比較提高慣性矩的補償幅度，說明靜態位移符合預期為何仍不能取代動態驗證。 再以本單元 L 的對照值重算 deflection，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Increase span while keeping the section fixed, calculate the compensating inertia change, and explain why agreement in static deflection cannot replace dynamic verification. Also recalculate deflection for the alternative L value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\"?","options":["在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點"],"optionsEn":["Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b309-v16-28","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 若卸載後仍有位移，須區分基座滑移與構件殘留變形。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. Residual displacement after unloading requires distinguishing fixture slip from permanent structural deformation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：量測橋跨與支點位移，避免把支承移動當成梁剛度改變。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Measure span and support motion to avoid mistaking support displacement for a stiffness change.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 若卸載後仍有位移，須區分基座滑移與構件殘留變形。","textEn":"Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. Residual displacement after unloading requires distinguishing fixture slip from permanent structural deformation.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater."],"answer":1,"explanation":"支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b309-v16-29","title":"集水與排水容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「集水與排水容量」如何影響九州新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kyushu Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。鐵路集水範圍若只算軌道面，會漏掉坡面與站區流入。 合理化流量法假定雨強與集流條件相符，面積及逕流係數也須明確。它估算峰值流率而非完整洪水歷線；抽水或蓄水設計還需對時間積分和出口條件。 以坡面集水和站口集水不同面積建立入流量比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「集水與排水容量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient. Actual drainage also depends on inlet blockage, pipe slope and downstream water level. Counting only track surface can omit inflow from adjacent slopes and station areas. The rational estimate assumes rainfall intensity compatible with catchment response and explicit area and runoff coefficient. It gives a peak rate, not a complete hydrograph. Pumping or storage design additionally requires time integration and outlet conditions. Compare inflow from a hillside catchment and a station entrance using their different areas. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.02e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.30906 m^3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.02e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.30906 m^3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「集水與排水容量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-29-k1","title":"集水與排水容量","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity","text":"短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。鐵路集水範圍若只算軌道面，會漏掉坡面與站區流入。","textEn":"A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient. Actual drainage also depends on inlet blockage, pipe slope and downstream water level.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「集水與排水容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\" is correct?","options":["排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位","量到變電所輸出電壓正常就代表所有列車端電壓正常","短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.","Normal substation output voltage proves that every train receives normal voltage.","A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient."],"answer":2,"explanation":"短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b309-v16-30","title":"集水與排水容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「集水與排水容量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.02e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.30906 m^3/s。敏感度：rain 單獨增加百分之十至 2.222e-05 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 0.339966 m^3/s。模型邊界：均勻降雨的合理化法概念；不含集流時間、水文頻率分析或蓄滯。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.02e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.30906 m^3/s. Sensitivity: rain, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2.222e-05 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.339966 m^3/s. Model boundary: Uniform-rainfall rational-method concept; concentration time, frequency analysis and storage are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.02e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.30906 m^3/s。敏感度：rain 單獨增加百分之十至 2.222e-05 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 0.339966 m^3/s。模型邊界：均勻降雨的合理化法概念；不含集流時間、水文頻率分析或蓄滯。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.02e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.30906 m^3/s. Sensitivity: rain, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2.222e-05 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.339966 m^3/s. Model boundary: Uniform-rainfall rational-method concept; concentration time, frequency analysis and storage are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「集水與排水容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.02e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2。","長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動","只要列車裝有再生煞車全部動能都能回到電網"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent.","Installing regenerative braking returns all train kinetic energy to the supply network."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.02e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.30906 m^3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.02e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.30906 m^3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b309-v16-31","title":"集水與排水容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「集水與排水容量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。 核對雨量單位和有效集水邊界，量測泵浦出流與集水井水位變化，以體積守恆互證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater. Verify rainfall units and catchment boundaries, measure pump outflow and sump-level change, and cross-check them through volume conservation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將部分入口視為堵塞，建立地表暫存與排出的水量表；比較增加入口和增加泵量對不同瓶頸的效果。 再以本單元 rain 的對照值重算 flow，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Block selected inlets in the scenario, tabulate surface storage and discharge, and compare additional inlets with additional pumping for different bottlenecks. Also recalculate flow for the alternative rain value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。 核對雨量單位和有效集水邊界，量測泵浦出流與集水井水位變化，以體積守恆互證。","textEn":"Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater. Verify rainfall units and catchment boundaries, measure pump outflow and sump-level change, and cross-check them through volume conservation.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將部分入口視為堵塞，建立地表暫存與排出的水量表；比較增加入口和增加泵量對不同瓶頸的效果。 再以本單元 rain 的對照值重算 flow，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Block selected inlets in the scenario, tabulate surface storage and discharge, and compare additional inlets with additional pumping for different bottlenecks. Also recalculate flow for the alternative rain value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「集水與排水容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。","任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater.","Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b309-v16-32","title":"集水與排水容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「集水與排水容量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 排水堵塞改變有效出流，不能只用較大泵浦銘牌值補償。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. Blocked drainage changes effective outflow and cannot be compensated merely by a larger pump nameplate rating. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以坡面集水和站口集水不同面積建立入流量比較。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare inflow from a hillside catchment and a station entrance using their different areas.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 排水堵塞改變有效出流，不能只用較大泵浦銘牌值補償。","textEn":"Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. Blocked drainage changes effective outflow and cannot be compensated merely by a larger pump nameplate rating.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「集水與排水容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","量到變電所輸出電壓正常就代表所有列車端電壓正常","垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Normal substation output voltage proves that every train receives normal voltage.","Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause."],"answer":2,"explanation":"垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b309-v16-s5","title":"牽引饋線壓降與可用度與修復時間","titleEn":"Traction feeder voltage drop & Availability and repair time","description":"本階段聚焦「牽引饋線壓降」與「可用度與修復時間」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Traction feeder voltage drop\" and \"Availability and repair time\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b309-v16-33","title":"牽引饋線壓降：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Traction feeder voltage drop: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「牽引饋線壓降」如何影響九州新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Traction feeder voltage drop” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kyushu Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"牽引電流經導體與回流路徑產生壓降，電壓下降又可能讓定功率列車要求更大電流，形成非線性負荷互動。單一電阻模型先隔離線路損耗，再逐步引入雙端供電和多列車位置。 回路電阻必須包含饋電與回流路徑，還需說明是否納入接頭和變電站等效阻抗。電流固定是簡化；實際定功率負載在電壓降低時可能增加電流並擴大壓降。 在爬坡高電流時估算供電壓降並核對回路定義。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「牽引饋線壓降」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Current through the feeder and return path creates voltage drop. A constant-power train may draw more current as voltage falls, creating nonlinear load interaction. A single resistance model first isolates line loss before adding two-ended supply and multiple train positions. Loop resistance must include supply and return paths, with joints and substation equivalent impedance explicitly included or excluded. Fixed current is a simplification: a constant-power load can draw more current as voltage falls and thereby increase the drop. Estimate voltage drop during high-current climbing and verify the defined electrical loop. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Traction feeder voltage drop” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：current=1515 A; resistance=0.06 ohm；計算：drop=current*resistance=90.9 V。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: current=1515 A; resistance=0.06 ohm; calculation: drop=current*resistance=90.9 V.","failure":"常見誤解：「量到變電所輸出電壓正常就代表所有列車端電壓正常」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Normal substation output voltage proves that every train receives normal voltage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「牽引饋線壓降」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Traction feeder voltage drop”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-33-k1","title":"牽引饋線壓降","titleEn":"Traction feeder voltage drop","text":"牽引電流經導體與回流路徑產生壓降，電壓下降又可能讓定功率列車要求更大電流，形成非線性負荷互動。單一電阻模型先隔離線路損耗，再逐步引入雙端供電和多列車位置。","textEn":"Current through the feeder and return path creates voltage drop. A constant-power train may draw more current as voltage falls, creating nonlinear load interaction.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：量到變電所輸出電壓正常就代表所有列車端電壓正常 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Normal substation output voltage proves that every train receives normal voltage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「牽引饋線壓降」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Traction feeder voltage drop\" is correct?","options":["牽引電流經導體與回流路徑產生壓降，電壓下降又可能讓定功率列車要求更大電流，形成非線性負荷互動。","量到變電所輸出電壓正常就代表所有列車端電壓正常","設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低"],"optionsEn":["Current through the feeder and return path creates voltage drop.","Normal substation output voltage proves that every train receives normal voltage.","High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low."],"answer":0,"explanation":"牽引電流經導體與回流路徑產生壓降，電壓下降又可能讓定功率列車要求更大電流，形成非線性負荷互動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Current through the feeder and return path creates voltage drop. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b309-v16-34","title":"牽引饋線壓降：定量估算","titleEn":"Traction feeder voltage drop: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「牽引饋線壓降」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Traction feeder voltage drop” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：current=1515 A; resistance=0.06 ohm；計算：drop=current*resistance=90.9 V。敏感度：current 單獨增加百分之十至 1666.5 A，其餘固定，結果為 99.99 V。模型邊界：固定電流與集中等效電阻；不含回生、功率因數與暫態。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: current=1515 A; resistance=0.06 ohm; calculation: drop=current*resistance=90.9 V. Sensitivity: current, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1666.5 A, with all other inputs fixed, gives 99.99 V. Model boundary: Fixed current and lumped equivalent resistance; regeneration, power factor and transients are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測變電所與列車端電壓及電流，記錄列車位置，將接頭接觸電阻與導體溫度造成的變化分別辨識。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronise substation and train voltage and current measurements, log train position, and distinguish joint contact resistance from conductor-temperature changes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：current=1515 A; resistance=0.06 ohm；計算：drop=current*resistance=90.9 V。敏感度：current 單獨增加百分之十至 1666.5 A，其餘固定，結果為 99.99 V。模型邊界：固定電流與集中等效電阻；不含回生、功率因數與暫態。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: current=1515 A; resistance=0.06 ohm; calculation: drop=current*resistance=90.9 V. Sensitivity: current, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1666.5 A, with all other inputs fixed, gives 99.99 V. Model boundary: Fixed current and lumped equivalent resistance; regeneration, power factor and transients are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「牽引饋線壓降」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Traction feeder voltage drop\", which statement holds?","options":["電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：current=1515 A; resistance=0.06 ohm。","煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion.","Original hypothetical exercise.","A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：current=1515 A; resistance=0.06 ohm；計算：drop=current*resistance=90.9 V。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: current=1515 A; resistance=0.06 ohm; calculation: drop=current*resistance=90.9 V. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b309-v16-35","title":"牽引饋線壓降：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Traction feeder voltage drop: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「牽引饋線壓降」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Traction feeder voltage drop” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測變電所與列車端電壓及電流，記錄列車位置，將接頭接觸電阻與導體溫度造成的變化分別辨識。 同步量測供電端與受電端電壓及回路電流，核對接線極性和設備接頭的額外壓降。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronise substation and train voltage and current measurements, log train position, and distinguish joint contact resistance from conductor-temperature changes. Measure supply voltage, receiving voltage and loop current synchronously, checking polarity and extra voltage drops across equipment connections. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：加入第二列同時加速的列車，畫出共享與非共享饋線段，分段重算壓降並說明何時需改用完整潮流分析。 再以本單元 current 的對照值重算 drop，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Add a second accelerating train, distinguish shared and separate feeder sections, recalculate each drop, and explain when a complete load-flow analysis becomes necessary. Also recalculate drop for the alternative current value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：高阻接頭可能在總壓降看似可接受時局部過熱；把導體長度和回流路徑計算一半會系統性低估損耗。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A high-resistance joint may overheat while total drop looks modest; omitting part of the return path systematically understates resistance and losses. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測變電所與列車端電壓及電流，記錄列車位置，將接頭接觸電阻與導體溫度造成的變化分別辨識。 同步量測供電端與受電端電壓及回路電流，核對接線極性和設備接頭的額外壓降。","textEn":"Synchronise substation and train voltage and current measurements, log train position, and distinguish joint contact resistance from conductor-temperature changes. Measure supply voltage, receiving voltage and loop current synchronously, checking polarity and extra voltage drops across equipment connections.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"加入第二列同時加速的列車，畫出共享與非共享饋線段，分段重算壓降並說明何時需改用完整潮流分析。 再以本單元 current 的對照值重算 drop，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Add a second accelerating train, distinguish shared and separate feeder sections, recalculate each drop, and explain when a complete load-flow analysis becomes necessary. Also recalculate drop for the alternative current value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「牽引饋線壓降」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Traction feeder voltage drop\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下","同步量測變電所與列車端電壓及電流，記錄列車位置，將接頭接觸電阻與導體溫度造成的變化分別辨識。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.","Synchronise substation and train voltage and current measurements, log train position, and distinguish joint contact resistance from conductor-temperature changes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步量測變電所與列車端電壓及電流，記錄列車位置，將接頭接觸電阻與導體溫度造成的變化分別辨識。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronise substation and train voltage and current measurements, log train position, and distinguish joint contact resistance from conductor-temperature changes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b309-v16-36","title":"牽引饋線壓降：失效診斷","titleEn":"Traction feeder voltage drop: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「牽引饋線壓降」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Traction feeder voltage drop” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高阻接頭可能在總壓降看似可接受時局部過熱；把導體長度和回流路徑計算一半會系統性低估損耗。 需核對回流路徑，否則可能把接頭故障藏在錯估電阻中。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A high-resistance joint may overheat while total drop looks modest; omitting part of the return path systematically understates resistance and losses. Verify the return path so a faulty connection is not hidden inside an incorrect resistance estimate. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在爬坡高電流時估算供電壓降並核對回路定義。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Estimate voltage drop during high-current climbing and verify the defined electrical loop.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「量到變電所輸出電壓正常就代表所有列車端電壓正常」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Normal substation output voltage proves that every train receives normal voltage.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高阻接頭可能在總壓降看似可接受時局部過熱；把導體長度和回流路徑計算一半會系統性低估損耗。 需核對回流路徑，否則可能把接頭故障藏在錯估電阻中。","textEn":"A high-resistance joint may overheat while total drop looks modest; omitting part of the return path systematically understates resistance and losses. Verify the return path so a faulty connection is not hidden inside an incorrect resistance estimate.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「牽引饋線壓降」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Traction feeder voltage drop\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["高阻接頭可能在總壓降看似可接受時局部過熱；把導體長度和回流路徑計算一半會系統性低估損耗。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低"],"optionsEn":["A high-resistance joint may overheat while total drop looks modest; omitting part of the return path systematically understates resistance and losses.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高阻接頭可能在總壓降看似可接受時局部過熱；把導體長度和回流路徑計算一半會系統性低估損耗。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A high-resistance joint may overheat while total drop looks modest; omitting part of the return path systematically understates resistance and losses. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b309-v16-37","title":"可用度與修復時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Availability and repair time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「可用度與修復時間」如何影響九州新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Availability and repair time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kyushu Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"在簡化更新過程中，可用度是平均故障間隔占故障間隔加修復時間的比例。這個指標不能替代安全性，因為快速恢復服務可能仍保留危險失效；備品、交通與診斷都會影響實際修復時間。 平均故障間隔和平均修復時間必須使用相同服務邊界；備件等待與到場時間若被排除，數字就不能描述旅客看到的中斷。短期樣本也應報告事件數與觀測時間。 對設備停機建立修復時間分布，分析單一平均值的限制。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「可用度與修復時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In a simplified renewal process, availability is mean time between failures divided by that time plus mean repair time. It does not replace safety: rapidly restoring service may leave a hazardous failure unresolved. Spares, travel and diagnosis all affect actual restoration time. Mean time between failures and mean repair time require a common service boundary. Excluding spare-part waiting or travel time prevents the figure from describing passenger-visible interruption. Short samples should also report event count and observation duration. Build a repair-duration distribution and examine the limits of representing downtime with one mean. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Availability and repair time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mtbf=1212 h; mttr=4 h；計算：availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9967105 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mtbf=1212 h; mttr=4 h; calculation: availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9967105 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「可用度與修復時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Availability and repair time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-37-k1","title":"可用度與修復時間","titleEn":"Availability and repair time","text":"在簡化更新過程中，可用度是平均故障間隔占故障間隔加修復時間的比例。這個指標不能替代安全性，因為快速恢復服務可能仍保留危險失效；備品、交通與診斷都會影響實際修復時間。","textEn":"In a simplified renewal process, availability is mean time between failures divided by that time plus mean repair time. It does not replace safety: rapidly restoring service may leave a hazardous failure unresolved.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「可用度與修復時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Availability and repair time\" is correct?","options":["設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低","在簡化更新過程中，可用度是平均故障間隔占故障間隔加修復時間的比例。","長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動"],"optionsEn":["High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low.","In a simplified renewal process, availability is mean time between failures divided by that time plus mean repair time.","One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在簡化更新過程中，可用度是平均故障間隔占故障間隔加修復時間的比例。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In a simplified renewal process, availability is mean time between failures divided by that time plus mean repair time. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b309-v16-38","title":"可用度與修復時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Availability and repair time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「可用度與修復時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Availability and repair time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mtbf=1212 h; mttr=4 h；計算：availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9967105 1。敏感度：mtbf 單獨增加百分之十至 1333.2 h，其餘固定，結果為 0.9970087 1。模型邊界：兩狀態穩態平均模型；不含計畫維修、共同原因與降級服務品質。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mtbf=1212 h; mttr=4 h; calculation: availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9967105 1. Sensitivity: mtbf, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1333.2 h, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.9970087 1. Model boundary: Two-state steady-state mean model; planned maintenance, common causes and degraded service quality are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將故障開始、到場、診斷、修復及恢復服務分段記錄，明確定義可用狀態，避免把降級運轉與完整服務混算。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record failure onset, arrival, diagnosis, repair and service restoration separately, define the available state, and avoid mixing degraded operation with full service.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mtbf=1212 h; mttr=4 h；計算：availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9967105 1。敏感度：mtbf 單獨增加百分之十至 1333.2 h，其餘固定，結果為 0.9970087 1。模型邊界：兩狀態穩態平均模型；不含計畫維修、共同原因與降級服務品質。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mtbf=1212 h; mttr=4 h; calculation: availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9967105 1. Sensitivity: mtbf, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1333.2 h, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.9970087 1. Model boundary: Two-state steady-state mean model; planned maintenance, common causes and degraded service quality are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「可用度與修復時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Availability and repair time\", which statement holds?","options":["只要列車裝有再生煞車全部動能都能回到電網","任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mtbf=1212 h; mttr=4 h。"],"optionsEn":["Installing regenerative braking returns all train kinetic energy to the supply network.","Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mtbf=1212 h; mttr=4 h；計算：availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9967105 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mtbf=1212 h; mttr=4 h; calculation: availability=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)=0.9967105 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b309-v16-39","title":"可用度與修復時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Availability and repair time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「可用度與修復時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Availability and repair time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將故障開始、到場、診斷、修復及恢復服務分段記錄，明確定義可用狀態，避免把降級運轉與完整服務混算。 逐項對照故障開始、服務恢復與維修完成時間，公開排除項，並核對總觀測時數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record failure onset, arrival, diagnosis, repair and service restoration separately, define the available state, and avoid mixing degraded operation with full service. Cross-check fault start, service restoration and repair completion for each event, disclose exclusions, and verify total observed hours. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較提高故障間隔與縮短修復時間兩種措施，用同一故障定義重算，並列出可用度之外需要追蹤的危險失效指標。 再以本單元 mtbf 的對照值重算 availability，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare increasing failure interval with reducing repair time under one failure definition, and list hazardous-failure measures that must be tracked separately from availability. Also recalculate availability for the alternative mtbf value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：只縮短更換時間但備品仍缺貨，可用度未必改善；將延後報修時間排除也會讓數字看似漂亮卻失去代表性。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Shorter replacement time may not improve availability when spare parts remain unavailable; excluding reporting delays can also create an unrepresentative figure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將故障開始、到場、診斷、修復及恢復服務分段記錄，明確定義可用狀態，避免把降級運轉與完整服務混算。 逐項對照故障開始、服務恢復與維修完成時間，公開排除項，並核對總觀測時數。","textEn":"Record failure onset, arrival, diagnosis, repair and service restoration separately, define the available state, and avoid mixing degraded operation with full service. Cross-check fault start, service restoration and repair completion for each event, disclose exclusions, and verify total observed hours.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較提高故障間隔與縮短修復時間兩種措施，用同一故障定義重算，並列出可用度之外需要追蹤的危險失效指標。 再以本單元 mtbf 的對照值重算 availability，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare increasing failure interval with reducing repair time under one failure definition, and list hazardous-failure measures that must be tracked separately from availability. Also recalculate availability for the alternative mtbf value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「可用度與修復時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Availability and repair time\"?","options":["將故障開始、到場、診斷、修復及恢復服務分段記錄，明確定義可用狀態，避免把降級運轉與完整服務混算。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Record failure onset, arrival, diagnosis, repair and service restoration separately, define the available state, and avoid mixing degraded operation with full service.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將故障開始、到場、診斷、修復及恢復服務分段記錄，明確定義可用狀態，避免把降級運轉與完整服務混算。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record failure onset, arrival, diagnosis, repair and service restoration separately, define the available state, and avoid mixing degraded operation with full service. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b309-v16-40","title":"可用度與修復時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Availability and repair time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b309-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「可用度與修復時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Availability and repair time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只縮短更換時間但備品仍缺貨，可用度未必改善；將延後報修時間排除也會讓數字看似漂亮卻失去代表性。 修好設備和恢復服務可能不同時，須分別記錄終點。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Shorter replacement time may not improve availability when spare parts remain unavailable; excluding reporting delays can also create an unrepresentative figure. Equipment repair and service restoration may occur at different times; record both endpoints. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：對設備停機建立修復時間分布，分析單一平均值的限制。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Build a repair-duration distribution and examine the limits of representing downtime with one mean.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「設備可用度高就表示所有安全風險一定很低」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"High equipment availability necessarily means every safety risk is low.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b309-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只縮短更換時間但備品仍缺貨，可用度未必改善；將延後報修時間排除也會讓數字看似漂亮卻失去代表性。 修好設備和恢復服務可能不同時，須分別記錄終點。","textEn":"Shorter replacement time may not improve availability when spare parts remain unavailable; excluding reporting delays can also create an unrepresentative figure. Equipment repair and service restoration may occur at different times; record both endpoints.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b309-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「可用度與修復時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Availability and repair time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只縮短更換時間但備品仍缺貨，可用度未必改善；將延後報修時間排除也會讓數字看似漂亮卻失去代表性。","長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Shorter replacement time may not improve availability when spare parts remain unavailable.","One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只縮短更換時間但備品仍缺貨，可用度未必改善；將延後報修時間排除也會讓數字看似漂亮卻失去代表性。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Shorter replacement time may not improve availability when spare parts remain unavailable; excluding reporting delays can also create an unrepresentative figure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-b309-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b309-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b309-en.svg"}};
